ices. <source>Br J Gen Pract</source><year>2000</year>;<volume>50</volume>:<fpage>892</fpage>-7.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11141876</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref53"><label>53</label><citation citation-type="journal">Fleissig A. Patients are frightened and their information needs fluctuate. <source>BMJ</source><year>2000</year>;<volume>321</volume>:<fpage>632</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="ref54"><label>54</label><citation citation-type="journal">Edwards A, Elwyn G. Inside the black box of shared decision making&#x02014;distinguishing between the process of involvement and who makes the decision. <source>Health Expect</source><year>2006</year>;<volume>9</volume>:<fpage>307</fpage>-20.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17083558</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list><notes notes-type="citation-text"><p><bold>Cite this as:</bold> <italic>BMJ</italic> 2008;337:a485</p></notes></back></article>